Algorithm: Student Certificate Upload Portal

Step 1: Start the application.

Step 2: Display the Student Certificate Upload Portal.

Step 3: Accept the following details from the student:

Roll Number

Name

Year

Section

Certificate Type

Certificate Title

Issuing Authority

Date of Certificate

Certificate File

Step 4: Check whether all required fields are entered.

Step 5: Check whether the certificate date belongs to the current month and current year.

Step 6: If the date is invalid, display an error message and stop the upload process.

Step 7: If the date is valid, access the parent folder in Google Drive.

Step 8: Search for a subfolder matching the selected certificate type.

Step 9: If the folder exists, select it; otherwise, create a new folder.

Step 10: Convert the uploaded Base64 data into a file blob.

Step 11: Rename the certificate using the student's Roll Number and file extension.

Step 12: Upload the certificate into the selected Google Drive folder.

Step 13: Format the certificate date into DD-MM-YYYY format.

Step 14: Open the Google Spreadsheet and append the student details.

Step 15: Display the success message.

Step 16: If an exception occurs, display an error message.

Step 17: Stop.
